{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01840",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.03,
      "end_seconds": 3.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.23,
      "end_seconds": 5.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Hello, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.9,
      "end_seconds": 9.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.16,
      "end_seconds": 27.69,
      "duration_seconds": 14.53,
      "text": "Ah, honestly, it's a purple rash that does not fade, and my family pushed me to come. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.3,
      "end_seconds": 32.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Alright, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.29,
      "end_seconds": 37.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Let me think, ever since... since yesterday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.59,
      "end_seconds": 42.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.19,
      "end_seconds": 67.01,
      "duration_seconds": 23.82,
      "text": "It, It feels mild to me. Yeah, I've also had a high fever, for three weeks. With high fever, it happens once or twice a day. And cold hands and feet, too. About cold hands and feet, mostly mild. Actually, and there's being drowsy as well, about a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.36,
      "end_seconds": 71.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.44,
      "end_seconds": 74.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 75.63,
      "end_seconds": 81.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 97, blood pressure 116 over 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.55,
      "end_seconds": 82.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.39,
      "end_seconds": 89.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.19,
      "end_seconds": 104.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Yes, uh, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.43,
      "end_seconds": 106.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.9,
      "end_seconds": 126.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "The purple spots do not fade when I press a glass on them, and he is floppy and drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.5,
      "end_seconds": 138.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Okay, thank you, you can get dressed. Have you had diarrhoea, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.22,
      "end_seconds": 141.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "No diarrhoea, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.6,
      "end_seconds": 147.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any stiff neck or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.97,
      "end_seconds": 150.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.52,
      "end_seconds": 155.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.61,
      "end_seconds": 158.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.7,
      "end_seconds": 163.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.53,
      "end_seconds": 167.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "My father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.2,
      "end_seconds": 171.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.1,
      "end_seconds": 183.95,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "Oh, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.52,
      "end_seconds": 188.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.72,
      "end_seconds": 200.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "I've had an irregular heartbeat for about a year now. Diabetes, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.72,
      "end_seconds": 207.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Yes. Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.36,
      "end_seconds": 227.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.05,
      "end_seconds": 239.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "It's apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day. Though honestly, some days I forget to take it. It's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 241.87,
      "end_seconds": 246.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.78,
      "end_seconds": 253.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.26,
      "end_seconds": 258.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.29,
      "end_seconds": 260.24,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.13,
      "end_seconds": 265.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.7,
      "end_seconds": 267.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.97,
      "end_seconds": 273.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.62,
      "end_seconds": 276.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.42,
      "end_seconds": 281.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.74,
      "end_seconds": 285.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.59,
      "end_seconds": 290.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.41,
      "end_seconds": 306.96,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I think we're dealing with possible meningococcal sepsis at this stage. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out a viral rash yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.01,
      "end_seconds": 323.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I'll request blood cultures, it'll help with possible sepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.22,
      "end_seconds": 325.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Mm, alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.49,
      "end_seconds": 351.56,
      "duration_seconds": 25.07,
      "text": "I think urgent blood tests makes sense here, for possible sepsis. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We'll begin with benzylpenicillin, 600 milligrams, once now, single dose. That should help with possible meningococcal sepsis. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.86,
      "end_seconds": 354.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.7,
      "end_seconds": 374.04,
      "duration_seconds": 18.34,
      "text": "I am giving an antibiotic injection now and calling an ambulance. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.99,
      "end_seconds": 381.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.03,
      "end_seconds": 393.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.64,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'll want another look straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.69,
      "end_seconds": 398.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Okay, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.63,
      "end_seconds": 403.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "How would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.69,
      "end_seconds": 413.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "So, I take the benzylpenicillin, 600 milligrams, once now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.17,
      "end_seconds": 420.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.53,
      "end_seconds": 425.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Well, great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.3,
      "end_seconds": 431.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Alright, all the best."
    }
  ]
}